  "limitations": [
    "Filename exclusions, rejection rather than recovery, continuation rejection and work limits are explicit broker policy; not every rejected value is forbidden by RFC syntax.",
    "Language well-formedness does not prove IANA registration, valid subtag prefixes or extension-specific semantics.",
    "Admitted filenames remain untrusted metadata. This does not establish filesystem/shell safety, safe file extensions, executable-content safety or authorization to write a file.",
    "RFC 6266 does not apply to MIME payload fields; their existing opaque Content-Disposition behavior remains separate and is not sanitized by this change.",
    "Unicode property agreement is verified for the current Python and Go runtimes, not promised for every future runtime version.",
